TEXT 112 -120 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
TEXT 112 -112 Left 2 !.options vntol=1m abstol=1m
TEXT 512 -96 Left 2 !x1 res1 res reset params: td1=10u td2=20u\nx2 res1 res2 reset params:td1=40u td2=50u\n \n* Device to reset a ltspice integrator (third parameter)\n* Reset has to be a 0-1-0 \n* note: td2 > td1 \n* in is a 0->1 and may also go later to 0 again \n.subckt reset in res params: td1=100u td2=200u\nA1 IN N001 0 0 0 0 res 0 AND Td={td1}\nA2 IN 0 0 0 0 N001 0 0 BUF Td={td2}\n* R1 Vx N001 100\n* V1 Vx 0 pwl 0s 1v\n.ends
TEXT 112 -64 Left 2 !b1 1 0 v=IDT(1,v(2),v(res2))\nb2 2 0 v=IDT(0,v(1)*0.5,v(res))
TEXT 112 -40 Left 2 ;1) res must be before res2 \n2) v(1) = Int(1) is reseted at the end of the integration\n3) The last value of v(1) multiplied by 0.5 (is memorized in the second integrator) \n     and is after reset of integrator2 = hold the old value fixed\n     given retour to integrator1 as new starting value\nb1 1 0 v=IDT(1,0.5*v(1),v(res2)) does not work\nbecause there will be first zeroed the integrator and than inited with the new (now) zerod value\nTherefore two integrators are necessary
TEXT -208 -136 Left 2 ;Exercise:\n \nThe integrator should integrate 1 and at reset point\nshould multiply output by 0.5 and restart with \nthis value the next integration period\nThis can only be done by two integrators:\nThe first integrate 1 \nThe second save the last value of integrator 1  before resetting him\nmultiply it by 0.5 and give it return to integrator 1 as new starting\nvalue\nNote res1 has to be before res because res set the new value at v(2)
